{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>When you come to the land.</b> This entry is different from all the entries in the Torah, for in all of them it says כִּי תָבֹא, כִּי תָבֹאוּ — therefore they all derive from one another, and since Scripture specified for you regarding one of them that it means nothing other than after inheritance and settlement, so too all of them. But this one says בְּבֹאֲכֶם — from the time they entered it and ate of its bread they became obligated in חַלָּה (Sifrei)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:11:02.097301674Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}